\label{thm:multi_snr_require_log_concave}
Consider the sensing matrix $\bX$ with its entries
$\bX_{i, j}$ being log-concave sub-gaussian RV with zero mean and unit variance
$(1\leq i \leq n, 1\leq j \leq p)$.
Assuming that $(i)$ $n\gg p^{1 + \varepsilon}\cdot\log^{3(1 +\varepsilon)} n\cdot \log^{2(1+\varepsilon)}(n^2 p^3)$
and  $(ii)$ $h\leq c_0 \cdot n$,
we can reliably obtain the permutation matrix with Algorithm~\ref{alg:one_step_estim}, namely,
$\Prob(\bPi^{\opt} = \bPi^{\natural}) \geq 1 - c_1 n^{-c_2} -c_3p^{-c_4}$,
in the following situations:
\begin{itemize}
\item
\textbf{Easy regime $(\srank{\bB^{\natural}} \gg \log^4 n)$}: we have $\snr \geq c$;

\item
\textbf{Medium regime $(\log n \ll \srank{\bB^{\natural}} \ll \log^4 n)$}:
we have $\log \snr \gsim \log \log n$;

\item
\textbf{Hard regime $(c(\varepsilon)\lsim \srank{\bB^{\natural}} \ll \log n)$}:
we have
\begin{align}
\label{eq:multi_snr_require_logconcave}	
\log \snr \gsim \frac{\log n}{\srank{\bB^{\natural}}} + \log \log n,
\end{align}
where $\varepsilon > 0$ is an arbitrary positive constant and
$c(\varepsilon)$ is a positive constant depending on $\varepsilon$.
\end{itemize}

\begin{align}
\label{eq:multi_snr_require_logconcave}	
\log \snr \gsim \frac{\log n}{\srank{\bB^{\natural}}} + \log \log n,
\end{align}

